        <mxCell id="flow-legend" value="Flow&#10;1. Corporate user resolves the public hosted zone&#10;2. Route 53 answers with the CloudFront distribution&#10;3. CloudFront origin fetch to the public ALB&#10;4. ALB routes to the AZ-a application tier&#10;5. ALB routes to the AZ-b application tier&#10;6. AZ-a application writes to the AZ-a writer&#10;7. AZ-b application writes to the AZ-b standby&#10;8. Synchronous cross-AZ database replication&#10;9. Application tier mounts the shared file system&#10;10. ALB ships access logs to the bucket (async)&#10;11. Database replicates to on-premises Oracle (async)" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#FFFFFF;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1490" y="120" width="380" height="212" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend" value="Legend&#10;Solid line = primary flow&#10;Dashed line = asynchronous / event-driven flow&#10;Red = blocked / missing / disabled&#10;🆕 = new in version N&#10;🔄 = changed in version N&#10;Dashed outer boundary = stack Boundary (profile brand color)&#10;Dashed inner boundary = Network Boundary (profile brand color)&#10;Numbered markers (1..N) = ordered data flow steps; see Flow list" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#FFFFFF;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10" vertex="1" parent="1">
